.TITLE "shutdown"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Enables you to shut down or restart local or remote computers. it is a critical tool for __system maintenance__ and __power management__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**shutdown /s**
Shuts down the local computer.
> __/s__ shutdown flag

**shutdown /r**
Shuts down and then restarts the local computer.
> __/r__ restart flag

**shutdown /a**
Aborts a system shutdown that has already been initiated.
> __/a__ abort flag

**shutdown /t 60**
Sets the time-out period before shutdown to 60 seconds.
> __/t 60__ timeout flag

**shutdown /h**
Puts the local computer into hibernation.
> __/h__ hibernate flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always warn other users on a multi-user system before initiating a shutdown. Using __shutdown /a__ is the only way to stop an accidental shutdown if a timeout was specified.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:taskkill** **windows:systeminfo**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/shutdown__
